   1.  DON'T DIE.  This is a bad sign even if you use an 
amulet of life saving.  Whatever kills you once can do it 
again.  Posts from users of amulets of life saving report
they either use them all, or don't use any.

   2.  This isn't Quake, so stop and think.

   3.  Marvin says (& I agree): 
        "Always have an escape route in mind." (generally
        to the upstairs.)

   4.  Know when to *use* the escape route. ;^)
   
   5.  Keep an escape item handy:
       - Scroll of teleportation (preferably either cursed
         or read while confused with teleport control.)
       - Wand of teleport (you or them)
       - Teleportitis  (activate with CTRL-T?)
       - Ring of teleportation (activate with CTRL-T?)
       - Means of engraving Elbereth
         - Finger
         - athame
         - disposable blade (;^)
         - wand of digging
         - wand of fire or lightning
       - Ring, potion, spell or boots of levitation to 
          float above finger engraved Elbereth to avoid 
          scuffing it while fighting or resting or
          spellcasting or quaffing or whatever.)
       - scroll of scare monster (pref blessed)
       - spell of cause fear
       - spell of charm monster
       - scroll of tame monster (preferably uncursed & read 
         while confused.)
       - blessed magic lamp
       - wand of wishing
       - cursed potion of gain level - nearest thing to 
         guaranteed.
       - blessed potion(s) of full healing
       - Orb of Fate (level teleport) - not recently invoked
       - Eye of Aethiopia (mine branch teleport) - not 
         recently invoked
       - #pray (not recently prayed)
       - magic whistle and monster pet

       The only 100% guaranteed method of escape is a cursed
       scroll of teleportation with teleport control.
       Even that needs to be protected from fire.


   6.  Learn to identify items so you'll know when you have
   an escape item and can use it in time.  There are posts
   from people who get a wish from a previously 
   un-identified wand just *before* they DYWYPI.


   7.  Know when to *use* the escape item.  The earlier you 
   use the item when you're in over your head, the better.
   (Except for the blessed potion of full healing.  Be sure
   it's not smoky or milky, too.)
  
     Get good enough at identifying dangerous situations &
   you'll be like Marvin, escaping without needing to use
   up an escape item.

     I think this is the main difference between ascending
   and not.  Note this requires knowing your current stats,
   weapons, skill levels, armor, resistances and inventory
   as well as the attacks, armor class, hit points, attack 
   points, resistances and special attacks of monsters.
    

   One last thing you need to learn is how to hit monsters
   and not get hit back.  Ranged attacks are a favorite.


